# Normalize line endings to LF in the repo and on checkout, regardless of the
# checking-out machine's `core.autocrlf`. Without this, a clone with
# `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git-for-Windows default) checks text files out as
# CRLF; icon-studio's `writeIfChanged` compares generated bytes exactly
# against what's on disk, so an LF-generated file would never match a
# CRLF-checked-out one, and Generate would report "written" on every run even
# when nothing actually changed.
* text=auto eol=lf
